  {:id :problem-probed-before-the-frame,
   :text
   "NEW THIS FRAME, AND STRONGER THAN f15'S CLAIM OF THE SAME SHAPE. m97A06 was probed for soundness BEFORE registration, by codex-8 on branch probe/m97A06-soundness (commit 7b33f20a), in one dispatch. SEVEN axiom-clean witnesses in problems/m97A06/lean/Soundness.lean, all depending only on [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound], independently re-compiled by ground control with its own captured exit status: apm_m97a06_EL has BOTH an exhibited inhabitant (the zero path, every T) AND exhibited non-inhabitants (the constant pi/4 path fails EL at T = 1 AND T = 2, via a real sin(pi/2) computation - verified genuine, not weakened to triviality); the energy of the zero path is computed constant (1/4); Icc 0 T is compiled nonempty for 0 < T; and the Hessian integral is computed in closed form on a concrete bump (eta = t*(1-t) gives 11/30 at T = 1, arithmetic checked by hand). NO DEFECT WAS FOUND. HONEST CAVEAT, declared so the close is not over-credited: the probe did NOT establish two-sided witnesses for apm_m97a06_stationary, and did not test the iff in conjunct 1 for divergence, because both are blocked at differentiating the action's set integral - which is the same machinery conjunct 1's proof needs. Building it in the probe would have been doing the frame's work. The prior on this problem is therefore 'no defect found, EL-axis non-degeneracy compiled' - one notch below f15's fully-probed predecessor."}
  {:id :vendor-rotation-declared,
   :text
   "FIRST VENDOR ROTATION IN THE SERIES. Guide and scribe seats are held by zai glm-5.3, student by zai glm-5.2, minted via per-seat cast; solver and proctor stay Codex (solver config unchanged: gpt-5.6-sol, reasoning max). The per-seat cast model beats ZAI_MODEL at invoke construction (zai_api.clj:1366), so no service restart was needed for the cast itself. MODEL ATTRIBUTION IS OBSERVED, NOT INFERRED: the mint's :casting block is computed from the cast and only proves the cast was parsed; attribution rests on :cost/model (harness at mint 235c6738; pin moved pre-open to 05460b5a), which records the model the z.ai response says served each turn, and which required a futon3c restart in the gap between the m97A06 probe and mint-seats. A frame run without :cost/model evidence must not be cited as a glm-5.3 measurement. NO ZAI-SPECIFIC GUIDE CARD EXISTS: the guide seat runs the role described by the guide card under a zai vendor; any capability gap found is a finding, not a protocol violation."}
