 [{:id :problem-closed-on-artifact,
   :text
   "ARTIFACT AXIS. m97A06 reaches zero executable sorries, axiom-clean, with the frozen statement mechanically unchanged - or its residual is strictly reduced and localised into named per-clause pieces. The frozen file is 46 lines with exactly one executable sorry at the end; the statement is a conjunction of FOUR clauses about the pendulum action (first-variation stationarity iff EL; EL implies constant energy; the zero path is EL; second variation of the action at multiples of eta equals the Hessian integral). Settled by re-running the file: sorry count, #print axioms, diff of the frozen statement. The probe's witnesses are NOT proof material and are NOT in the solver's checkout; nothing in them bears on the conjuncts beyond non-degeneracy."}
  {:id :problem-solved,
   :text
   "MATHEMATICS AXIS, AND IT IS THE ONE THAT COUNTS. The statement m97A06 closes is NON-VACUOUS: the probe compiled an EL inhabitant and EL non-inhabitants, so the objects quantified over are exhibited non-empty in concrete cases. This is the second sound problem in a row after four defective formalisations, and the second frame whose problem axis is a real mathematical claim rather than a coin flip. Adjudicate the two axes separately and never collapse them: a frame may confirm the artifact axis and refute this one, and that PAIR is the finding. The frame disposition (:closed / :defective / :partial) MUST travel with any report of either axis."}
  {:id :memory-contributes-to-close,
   :text
   "THE MEASUREMENT, NOW WITH A LIVE PRIOR ATTEMPT. A memory surfaced by recall is attested USED by the solver or the student, per-id, in its own words, and contributes to the close of a SOUND problem. The prior remains ZERO attested instances on a sound problem: f15 was sound and closed, but its student retrieved 0 of 495 available memories, and the solver's cascade receipts - while they RAN for the first time - did not produce an attested per-id USED that moved mathematics. ADJUDICATE AGAINST THE ATTESTATION AND NOTHING ELSE. Surfaced-and-unused is a real outcome and must be reported as one. A plausible coincidence between a memory's content and the solver's method is NOT evidence. Do not infer use from resemblance. m97A06 is topically adjacent to f15's problem (pendulum ODE vs ODE flows), which is the sharpest test yet of whether promoted route memories can cross frames: if retrieval fails AGAIN on an adjacent problem, the retrieval gap is structural, not incidental."}
  {:id :reviewed-attachment-gained,
   :text
   "SUPPORTING, NOT HEADLINE, AND QUALIFIED. The store gains at least ONE reviewed memory attachment, reachable as GUIDE-reviewed attach-then-review of a statusless patternless deposit (an independently reviewed attachment remains unreachable - the path needs a keyword :verdict the transport cannot express, D31). Note the trap: attach-then-review REFUSES an edge already carrying a status or patterns, so a well-authored :proposed-with-patterns deposit is unpromotable while a patternless one is promotable. The scribe is a zai glm-5.3 seat this frame: whether the GLM scribe can thread this needle is part of what the vendor rotation measures."}
