   :text
   ":memory-disposition-offer-ids is NON-EMPTY so runtime invariant F3 passes, as it did live for the first time in f15. The f15 caveat carries: the dispositions recorded only that offers EXISTED (:write-use takes no verdict), so a populated field is necessary and not sufficient - count only per-id attested dispositions as evidence of use."}
  {:id :guidance-count-exact,
   :text
   "The recorded guidance count EQUALS the true number of guidance bells sent, and in particular is 0 if none were sent. The GUIDE IS A GLM-5.3 SEAT THIS FRAME: a guidance-count anomaly under a zai guide is a vendor-rotation finding first and a protocol defect second."}
  {:id :glm-seats-complete-the-frame,
   :text
   "NEW THIS FRAME, AND IT IS WHAT THE ROTATION EXISTS TO MEASURE. The zai guide and scribe (glm-5.3) and student (glm-5.2) seats each complete their frame role without a seat failure requiring ground control to substitute a Claude seat: the guide conducts orientation, ignition and adjudication; the scribe deposits at least one memory that reaches review; the student runs its lane and produces attested per-id dispositions. Seat attribution for every completed role is OBSERVED in :cost/model and matches the cast. A seat failure is not a protocol violation - it is the measurement. What is NOT permitted is attributing work to glm-5.3 without :cost/model evidence."}
  {:id :analyst-survives-two-frames,
   :text
   "analyst-3 completes duties A, B and F at this close. It is at TENURE 2 OF 2 and therefore OWES succession HERE: the handoff document, memory-surface pointer and W-entry fall due at THIS close, frame 16, its second and last. The f15 registration's copy of this text described the WRONG tenure (first, not last frame) and its successor prose was caught only by a fresh read - the generator's forbidden-token list was case-sensitive, so the lowercase stale tenure claim sailed through it. A prediction that cannot be satisfied or refuted by the frame it ships in is a defect in the prediction, not a result - report it as such if you meet one.\n"}
